#: ../../../lib/_autosummary/xompletions/xompletions.sudo.rst:2
msgid "xompletions.sudo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xompletions/sudo.py:docstring of xompletions.sudo:1
msgid "Completer for ``sudo``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xompletions/sudo.py:docstring of xompletions.sudo:3
msgid ""
"``sudo`` is more than a transparent command wrapper: it has its own flag "
"grammar, accepts ``VAR=value`` environment assignments before the command, "
"and honours the POSIX ``--`` end-of-options sentinel. The generic command-"
"token skipper in :mod:`xonsh.completers.commands` only knows how to strip "
"the literal ``sudo`` token, which leaves ``sudo -- foo``, ``sudo -u root "
"foo`` and similar invocations without useful completions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xompletions/sudo.py:docstring of xompletions.sudo:10
msgid ""
"This module walks ``ctx.args`` past every token that belongs to ``sudo``'s "
"own prefix (flags, their values, ``VAR=value`` assignments, ``--``) and then "
"either offers command names (when the cursor sits on the inner command word) "
"or re-enters the full completion pipeline with the inner command at "
"``args[0]`` so the inner command's own completers (``man``, paths, ``pip``'s "
"xompletion, …) surface."
msgstr ""

